course: dictionary
lesson: 13459
title: Humanoid: shaped like a person
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Humanoid is built from two parts: human, meaning a person, and -oid, meaning like or shaped like. So a humanoid has a shape like a person's: a head, two arms, two legs, and it stands upright. It does not have to be a real person.
explain: «The humanoid robot picked up the cup and carried it to the table.» The robot is not a human, but its human shape lets it use the same chairs, doors and tools that people use. Try your meaning in the sentence. Does "shaped like a person" still make sense? Then it works.
explain: Humanoid can also be a noun, a thing itself: «The humanoids in the film had silver skin and walked just like us.» Here a humanoid is a robot, alien or creature that looks like a person. You may also see the phrases humanoid alien, humanoid form and humanoid shape.
fact: Humanoid means having a shape or features like a human being.
fact: As a noun, a humanoid is a robot, alien or creature that looks like a person.
fact: Humanoid robots are built in a human shape so they can use stairs, tools and doors made for people.
fact: In old books, humanoid can mean an early human-like species, but scientists today usually say «hominin» or «hominid».
fact: The word parts show the meaning: human plus -oid (like or shaped like) makes humanoid.
exercise: «The humanoid robot walked across the lab on two legs.» What does humanoid mean here? | Made of wood and painted green | *Shaped like a person, with a head, arms and legs | Very fast, like a racing car | Able to fly through the air
exercise: In a science lesson, why are humanoid robots built with a human shape? | *So they can use stairs, tools and doors made for people | To make them smaller and lighter | To swim under the sea | Because the shape is the most popular colour
exercise: In «The humanoid robot waved hello», what kind of word is humanoid? | Noun | Verb | Pronoun | *Adjective
test: «The film showed a humanoid alien with green skin and two arms.» What does humanoid mean here? | *A creature that looks roughly like a person | A plant that grows in water | A rock from the Moon | A type of spaceship
test: Scientists today usually use which word for early human-like species? | Robot | Humanoid robot | Alien | *Hominin
exam: «The humanoid robot had a head, two arms and two legs, and it walked upright.» Which feature shows the robot is humanoid? | *Its head, two arms and two legs | Its wheels | Its bright colour | Its battery
